.TH RAYLIB 2
.SH NAME
raylib \- native game and multimedia library
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <u.h>
.br
.B #include <libc.h>
.br
.B #include <raylib.h>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Raylib provides window input, 2D drawing, images, text, 3D models,
cameras, collision tests and audio. This port uses the native C compiler
and libraries. Compile clients with the
.B -p
option; the header selects
.B libraylib.a
at link time.
.PP
Graphics programs run inside a
.IR rio (4)
window. The classic OpenGL renderer uses
.IR tinygl (2)
and VirGL through
.IR gpu (3).
Frames are copied into the window with
.IR draw (2).
Keyboard, mouse, clipboard and URLs use the native files and plumber.
Window and cursor operations obey rio's focus and placement policy.
.PP
Audio uses a shared-memory mixer process writing signed 16-bit stereo PCM
at 44100 Hz to
.BR /dev/audio .
Release sounds and streams before closing the audio device. Audio callbacks
run under the mixer lock and must not reenter APIs that acquire that lock.
.PP
The public headers document the API.
.B <raymath.h>
provides vector and matrix helpers;
.B <rlgl.h>
exposes the compiled classic rendering interface.
Clients must not define
.BR RLGL_IMPLEMENTATION .
For matrix arrays, store the result of
.B MatrixToFloatV
in a named
.B float16
and use its
.B v
member.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /sys/src/libraylib/README
Build instructions, tests and native constraints.
.TP
.B /sys/src/libraylib/examples
Self-contained rotating textured cube demo; run
.B mk install
then
.BR games/raydemo .
Space pauses, arrows orbit, and the wheel zooms.
.B -a
adds a sound on Space;
.B -n
limits the number of frames.
.SH SOURCE
.B /sys/src/libraylib
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR tinygl (2),
.IR draw (2),
.IR audio (3),
.IR gpu (3),
.IR rio (4)
.SH BUGS
The renderer implements the classic OpenGL path. Programmable shaders,
render textures, instancing and modern OpenGL examples are unavailable.
Targets are limited to 2048 by 2048 pixels. One window/context per process
is supported. Window icons, opacity, gamepads and clipboard images are
unavailable. Only amd64 with QEMU VirGL has been tested.
.PP
.B FileRename
supports renaming within one directory, including paths to that directory.
